{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/170697-populations","id":170697,"title":"Populations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-16T07:19:29-07:00","id":170697,"title":"Populations","content":"This is a post that doesn't really have a home anywhere (being about all of the World of Darkness), but I'm putting it in my favourite sub-forum.<br /> <br /> So, has anyone tried to do a rough estimation of populations? <br /> <br /> Before I go on, I realise this is a ludicrous thing to attempt, but it's more curiosity. I get the feeling Sin Eaters are quite rare, compared to Vampires say. But how do the others stack up?<br /> <br /> Anyone want to hazard a list of how common a race is to uncommon? Or even go that extra step, and say how many (1 in 10000 etc)?<br /> <br /> Like it said, ludicrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T07:53:15-07:00","id":170727,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about specific populations, but one thing I would suggest is there's robably a more even parity between older and younger Sin-Eaters number wise. Between their ectoplasmic resilience and their resurrection capabilities, there would probably a lower (permanent) death rate amongst the Bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T08:53:20-07:00","id":170789,"title":"","content":"Matt McFarland has mentioned that most of Promethean's material was written under the assumption put forward in Mortal Remains that there's less than a hundred of the Created on Earth at any given time.<br /> <br /> Werewolf Core puts forward the approximate headcount of Uratha (Forsaken and Pure combined) as &quot;less than half a million.&quot; This may or may not hold true after a little south of a decade of line progression.<br /> <br /> The nature of mages makes it difficult to get an exact headcount, though the relative figures for the major organizations are that:<br /> \u2022 The Free Council is the largest unified subgroup of non-Nameless mages.<br /> \u2022 The Guardians of the Veil are the smallest unified subgroup of non-Nameless mages.<br /> \u2022 The Seers of the Throne, with all their Ministries combined, have about as many members as two of the remaining three Pentacle Orders<br /> \u2022 The most common estimates say there are twice as many Pentacle mages as Seers.<br /> <br /> Vampire and changeling populations vary widely from city to city based on population and immigration/emigration figures, respectively, as well as the laws of the local Prince for the former and the number of trods in town for the latter.<br /> <br /> There are, in all probability, fewer than a thousand of the Arisen in existence overall, and far fewer of these awake at the same time after accounting for a century or two of variance between individual Sothic Turns.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eater population may or may not fluctuate wildly in response to massive outbreaks of the things the Horsemen represent - war, famine, plague, disasters both natural and unforeseen - but the headcount needed to manage the creation of a Conspiracy-level krewe, in combination with the increased survivability of the Bound, suggests the total is somewhere in between the figures for werewolves and mummies, if not Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T09:44:10-07:00","id":170822,"title":"","content":"I wrote Mortal Remains Geist section under the assumption Sin-Eaters are rare and few hunters will ever meet one. Going with Sach's comment, I also assumed certain eras had &quot;spikes&quot; in their population in specific areas...such as World War II in Europe.<br /> <br /> The below is of course unofficial speculation<br /> <br /> The modern world is no paradise. There is war, disease, famine, all that. But I wager the number of Sin-Eaters around right now is fairly low, especially in the West, and even parts of Asia. The modern world, compared to any previous era in history, is, taken as a world whole, pretty damn nice. I'd estimate the 1940s saw possibly 1.5 to twice the number of Sin-Eaters we have now, and that they were definitely more common in the 19th Century than the twentieth outside the World War eras.<br /> <br /> This would explain the reletive lack of Tier Three Krewes now, at least in the West. I'd place Sin-Eater numbers closer to Mummy numbers than anything else worldwide. Almost Certainly more Sin-Eaters (especially counting African Sin-Eaters) than Mummies, but still.<br /> <br /> Just a few thoughts on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T10:13:00-07:00","id":170837,"title":"","content":"My personal view is that Sin-Eaters should be pretty damn common. The reason being is that the more krewes around, the more colorful and diverse the local Bound are, the happier I am. That takes a lot of Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though I acknowladge that Baron Samedi is completely correct about the cannon. Though 1.5 - 2 times for WWII is quite low if you ask me. And also, in a hunter game I'd make Sin-Eaters a lot rarer than in a Geist game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T11:11:02-07:00","id":170896,"title":"","content":"I'd certainly back the idea that the more Krewes around, the more colorful and diverse the local Bound are! Lots of fun stuff to do there, though I've been doing it via groups of mortals around some Bound to give a sense of scale without having a shit-ton of Sin Eaters around. Having lots of Sin-Eaters would certainly make things exciting, though.<br /> <br /> Are there any Hunter estimates, especially for Conspiracy or Compact level organizations? I could have sworn I read once that TF:V have 6,000 members, 2,000 of which were field agents, but I can't for the life of me find that number again.<br /> <br /> Those Mage estimates are. . .really interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T11:29:23-07:00","id":170926,"title":"","content":"That number is in the corebook; but it always seemed wrong to me. (Mind you, it might be the fact that TF:V was said to be bigger than the Ascending Ones)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T11:48:52-07:00","id":170938,"title":"","content":"I believe there's bit in the Changeling line that references the Lost as the most populous of all the major templates... but that the vast majority of them are in Arcadia. That could mean, though, that Fetches are the most numerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T15:40:07-07:00","id":171135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/170697-populations?p=170926#post170926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That number is in the corebook; but it always seemed wrong to me. (Mind you, it might be the fact that TF:V was said to be bigger than the Ascending Ones)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think TF:V as a whole is around three to five thousand but two thirds of that are support personal (Research, Admin, and Manufacturing) so you're only seeing about one third of that number on the ground at any given time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T08:28:00-07:00","id":171663,"title":"","content":"I figured the limiting factor on sin-eater population was the number of extant geists willing and able to make the bargain, not the number of violent and premature deaths. Because even in the most comparatively-idyllic location-periods in history (location is important: it's never idyllic everywhere), there are still going to be enough deaths for any geist who wants to walk the world to take their pick of hosts (if nothing else, being poor is usually a high-deathrate pasttime)<br /> <br /> As such, I would assume that sin-eater population would either be relatively stable, or at least that its peaks and valleys would be on a delay from any triggering real-world events: long enough for some percentage of the ghosts created by those events to get old and weird and turn into geists. If we assume that takes about a hundred years, then it makes sense that there'd be a big spike in sin-eaters about a century after any given tragedy, war, or period of tribulation. If we instead assume that it takes a thoroughly unpredictable number of years for a geist to &quot;mature&quot;, then you end up with slow swells after tragedies, which is an effect that looks more or less like stability if you don't analyze it really closely.<br /> <br /> Which is why I read the bit in mortal remains and assumed it referred to an increase in sin-eater <i>activity</i> rather than an increase in sin-eater <i>population. </i>Lots of death, lots to do, very busy, fewer parties, more ghost-busting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 06-17-2014, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T10:54:08-07:00","id":171771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/170697-populations?p=171135#post171135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think TF:V as a whole is around three to five thousand but two thirds of that are support personal (Research, Admin, and Manufacturing) so you're only seeing about one third of that number on the ground at any given time.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was that I feel TF:V + support personal &lt; Ascending Ones + support personal (e.g. an Ascending One gang leader, non-AO gang members)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T15:37:59-07:00","id":172088,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I think judgeing Sin-Eater by activity instead of number is a better way of going about. Unlike Vampires and Changelings who need to engage Mortals in order to restock their important resource, Mages who constantly run the risk of Abyssal intrusion if they use their Magic (which we all know they will) and Prometheans who destroy the world by their merest pressence, Sin-Eaters dont actually impact the Mortal society they inhabit very much. Perhaps the only indication is that the ghosts in the area will probably act alittle wierd at times, trying to get the Sin-Eaters attention and by more quiet at other times when the Bound have heeded them recently.<br /> Its very likely that nobody would really realise a Sin-Eater is a Sin-Eater unless circumstance seriously conspires to make it so.<br /> <br /> That said, the core Geist book makes it rather clear that Sin-Eaters are rare even by the standard of other supernaturals. So I'd probably make it all look something akin to this:<br /> <br /> Vampires &gt; Changelings &gt; Mages &gt; Werewolfs &gt; Sin-Eaters &gt; Prometheans<br /> <br /> Then its just a matter of determining how numerous supernaturals are in your scenario in general, and scaling things around that. I dont have the Mummy and Demon books, so I cant speak about their numbers. Also, this is entirely my own interpritation, not facts set in stone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T00:22:09-07:00","id":191179,"title":"","content":"I agree that they would be rather rare, but I personally believe that they are not exactly endangered, and with all probability thanks to the Good Baron and Mortal Remains, the recent travesties have lead to a recent surge in their numbers, and not just bound, but Geister creation as well, thanks to the huge influx of such complimentary and conflicting Essence, spirit/ghost predation as well as upheavals in the Underworld providing possibly emergence of catalysts for the acquiring of Thresholds and Keys would allow for numbers to at least grow by another 1.5x.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}